2 DATE ABT 28 FEB 1828
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1862
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was given the task of looking after a chapel in the hills of Ladera on the Sanches Hacienda. He lived adjacent to the chapel devoted to Saint Joseph, the family patron saint. The chapel was built by his father J
2 CONC uan Jose Sanchez and he instructed all the family Sanchez , present and future family to care maintain the chapel for their salvation.
2 CONT
2 CONT I was told by my aunt that the chapel  had burned and that Juan Jose Sanchez was able to save the santos and pictures and that Maria Manuela Sanchez had set up the santos and pictures in a room at the adobe hacienda so that family
2 CONC  and neighbors had a place to attend to their devotions. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1908 after Jesus Sanchez died, his son Uvaldo Isidor Sanchez sent out a letter asking for contributions in order to rebuild the chapel and reinstall the santos and pictures. He stated that he had been remiss at performing his r
2 CONC eligious duties and that they should all work toward the goals of rebuilding the chapel to insure their salvation. I have a copy of this letter, I do not know if it was ever rebuilt in the hills of Ladera, Valencia, New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Update:
2 CONT
2 CONT The chapel was rebuilt after 1908 by his nephew, Uvaldo Sanchez. Soon after his wife Rosela died in childbirth and her funeral was held at the chapel on the hacienda.
