1 NOTE {geni:about_me}      In his life time Juan de Dios had been a plainsman, a freighter, a buffalo hunter along the Santa Fe Trail. His life was closely linked with pioneer history of the southwest. He became a prosperous farmer and 
2 CONC rancher raising cattle and sheep.  He was a well known agricultural leader in Taos County.  He was an individual private banker in Arroyo Seco.  In politics he was a strong democrat and served as probate judge in 1901 and 1902.
