1 NAME Justiniano Hermenegildo /Sanchez/
2 GIVN Justiniano Hermenegildo
2 _MARNM Sanchez
2 NICK Joseph Herman Sanchez
1 NAME Justiniano Hermenegildo Sanchez (Joe Sanchez)
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Rose Hills Memorial Park
2 ADDR
3 CITY Whittier
3 STAE California
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1909
2 ADDR
3 CITY La Ladera de Valencia
3 STAE New Mexico
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1978
2 ADDR
3 CITY Los Angeles
3 STAE California
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Real Estate Investor
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Information from Joseph H Sanchez, grandson
2 CONT
2 CONT My grandfather grew up in Valencia, New Mexico and came to Los Angeles during the Great Depression in the 1930's along with his dad and his dad's three sisters and one brother. He followed them, rode box cars and played banjo alon
2 CONC g the way. He used the name Joseph Herman Sanchez when he joined the merchant marines during WWll, when he died we found out his real name was Justinano Hermengildo Sanchez. I found this strange since I was named after him and he 
2 CONC never mentioned it. He has the name Joseph H. Sanchez on his headstone at his grave-site which is not his given name.
2 CONT
2 CONT He settled in Los Angeles near the Dunbar Hotel In the South Central area and opened a lunch counter one block away from the Dunbar Hotel which served a black clientele.  He also ran a used car lot with a black partner. Later he o
2 CONC pened a donut shop, all his businesses were located in the black neighborhood of South Central. In the 1950's he finally tried his hand at real estate and opened a real estate office on Central Ave. with his brothers and started b
2 CONC uying rental properties and this was the business he was in until he died. When he died he had owned hundreds of rental properties during his life. His life was the rags to riches story of  America made  possible thru good luck, w
2 CONC hich my grandfather said was hard work and plenty of it. He was what you would call an odd character with a different sense of humor, his son, my father was also quite different and odd. My sister and I have a similar sense of hum
2 CONC or that is somewhat inherited from my grandfather, my other siblings do not.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died when he was sixty seven. I wish he had lived longer and had told me more about his family and life in New Mexico. I had to find out this history thru geni..com and research on the internet. And that story is the history of
2 CONC  the colonization of New Mexico in 1597 and the journey of the Spanish and the Sephardic  Jews,who came and settled the Mexican Northern Frontier and settled in New Mexico and stayed  there for over 400 years. The history of being
2 CONC  Jewish so suppressed that my family had no idea of a Jewish history that has been proven by my DNA results.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also is the history of the Mexican Indian wives that many of the men brought with them into New Mexico must not be forgotten. Spanish and also Sephardic men had married Mexican Indian wives and brought their children into New Mexi
2 CONC co. Later their sons and daughter would marry and have children with the Native Indians of New Mexico. Our family history is one of incredible struggle, endurance and survival of many cultures. 
