1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lawrence, or Sonny as we knew him, was first married to Grace who, coincidently ended up being my typing teacher in high school, but he seemed extraordinarily happy married to Lori, his second wife.  I see Lori fro
2 CONC m time-to-time as we both live in Santa Fe.  Sonny and my father, Errett Lujan, kept in touch - they were cousins.  Sonny's death was difficult on my dad and, especially on Lori and his immediate family.  Sonny died just before my
2 CONC  father, probably 1990.  I'll check on that with Lori.  Sonny died from a failed liver caused by Agent Orange in the Vietnam War.  He was a general in the US Army.  My father and I went to visit him about a month before he passed 
2 CONC away.  Although very ill, he talked with us a long time.  I believe he is buried at the National Cemetery here in Santa Fe.
2 CONT
