1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tranquelino Jose Archuleta, 85, of Mountainair, NM passed away June 16, 2006 in Mountainair, NM with his loving family beside him. Tranquelino was born November 24, 1920 in Mountainair, NM to Manuel and Altagracia 
2 CONC (Romero) Archuleta. Tranquelino worked for the Forest Services as a Ranger.Tranquelino married Estella Zamora in Willard, NM on November 9, 1945. He is survived by his sons, Markie and wife Pam Archuleta of Mountainair, NM; Juan a
2 CONC nd wife Michelle Archuleta of Mountainair, NM; LeRoy and wife Sandy Archuleta of Port Angles, Wa; Sam and wife Viola Archuleta, Mountainair, NM; daughters, Dubi and husband Norman Lindsey of Mountainair, NM; brothers, Filomeno Arc
2 CONC huleta; Filberto and wife Theresa Archuleta; sisters, Flora Chavez; 15 grandchildren; 33 great grandchildren. He was preceded in death by his wife Estella Archuleta; parents, Manuel and Altagracia Archuleta. Funeral Services will 
2 CONC be held Monday, June 19, 2006 at 2:00 PM at the First Assembly of God in Mountainair, NM Pastor Ed Rimer will be officiating; internment will follow at the Mountainair Cemetery in Mountainair, NM. Pallbearers will be Mateo Martine
2 CONC z, Francisco Martinez, Joe Archuleta, Tranquelino Archuleta, Adam Archuleta, and Tobias Archuleta. Honorary Pallbearers are Dimitri Karper, Uziah Sheppard, Dominic Martinez, Samuleto Archuleta, Damiel J. Archuleta, Christopher Can
2 CONC delaria, Cisco Martinez, and Fermian Ruiz.
