0 @N6000000005598936874@ NOTE Elena Gallegos picnic area is named for her, it is located in the western foothills of Sandia Mountains, New Mexico.
1 CONT She was the first woman to own a cattle brand.
0 @N6000000005598973883@ NOTE Baptised 2 April 1703. Bernallilo, Sandoval, NM.
1 CONT New Mexico Land Grants - Reel 38 - C51 - Frame 32, Elena Gallegos Grant
1 CONT
1 CONT Translation - Will of Antonio Gurule
1 CONT
1 CONT The will starts with confession of faith, with desire to be buried in a Franciscan habit near the front of the church. States that he, Antonio Gurule, is a resident of Albuquerque. Names as executors: his "son" Tadeo Garcia (husba
1 CONC nd of daughter Luisa) and his wife, Antonia Quintana - whom he wishes to be custodian of his property and guardian of his children.
1 CONT
1 CONT States that he has been married to Antonia Quintana for 40 years, and that they have had nine children: Tomas, Manuela, Luisa, Fabiana, Juan Antonio, Serafin, Elena, Francisca, and Manuelita; and that eight of them are married. To
1 CONC mas and the others have received what is coming to them by inheritance of land and other property and 300 acres of land for agriculture. He states that when he was married to his wife, he had nothing but the inheritance from his p
1 CONC arents.
1 CONT
1 CONT He states that he owns a tract of land called Jesus Maria on which he has some cultivated land and a house of six rooms and on the land a ditch for irrigation and that it should be understood that as legal owner, he gives half to 
1 CONC his wife and half to his children. He states that first a portion must be used to pay for his funeral expenses and debts and ___ something to _______ .
1 CONT
1 CONT He also states that two Indian women, Rosa and Elena, who had served his mother should be freed and provided for.
1 CONT
1 CONT He enumerated his property -- one saddle, one bridle, one sheath, one sword, one coat, two spurs, one horse and 2 yoke of oxen with yokes. He says that his son Serafin should have the gun, shield and sword and that his wife should
1 CONC  have the saddle, bridle, spurs, the cart and three beasts (horses and oxen). He states that he owes Marcos Baca 26 sheep and that he should be paid.
1 CONT
1 CONT He states that he has had of Bernardino Sena, resident of the Villa, 208 ____ only on good faith and he wants to honor this. He also stated that he gave Tomas de Sena, resident of the Villa, 60 sheep, on good faith, apparently the
1 CONC y were to share the lambs - after a year and two years. He would like this carried out. He wishes Bentura Mestas to take care of the loss or gain.
1 CONT
1 CONT He asks the Alcade Mayor, Capt Jose Xaramillo, to adjudicate the codicil and will and give the custody of his goods to Antonia Quintana. Signed by his own hand on 8 Apr 1761.
1 CONT
1 CONT Then he states Alexander Gonzales owes him one cow.
1 CONT
1 CONT Signed Antonio Grolet
1 CONT
1 CONT Witnesses: Jose Xaramillo, Judge
1 CONT
1 CONT Silvestre Griego
1 CONT
1 CONT Salvador Martinez
0 @N6000000005598760774@ NOTE Buried July 1, 1783, Albuquerque, Bernalillo, New Mexico, USA.
1 CONT Note: Jun 7, 1783 - di sepultura ecclesiatica a Maria Gertrudis Aragon, espanola, adulta, casada que era de Serafino Gurule, espanol, vecinos de esta Villa, y residentes de la Plaza de Gamboa.
0 @N6000000005598973915@ NOTE [Olmsted]  Elena Gurulé was the second wife of Jose Duran y Chavez of Bernalillo, to whom she was married about 1765.  When Chavez was accidentally killed in 1783, there ensued a lengthy succession (probate) process involving the 
1 CONC children of his first marriage.  Elena and Jose were the parents of nine children.
0 @N6000000005598973968@ NOTE Baptism: December 3, 1773 San Felipe, Albuquerque, Bernallilo Co., NM.
0 @N6000000005024502626@ NOTE Catholic
