1 CONT
1 CONT After his marriage, he moved his family to La Joya, south of Belen, N.M.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jose Miguel Hermenegildo Salas made his living raisinf cattle and sheep was well as a freighter.  He and his brothers-in law, Mathias and Alvino Contreras, were frequent traders on the Santa Fe and Chihuahua Trails. These three pl
1 CONC us other relatives served in the Civil war in the New Mexico Militia's Company G, First Regimen, Second Brigade, Third Division which was organized in La Joya under Captain Juan Carillo on December 12. 1863 and was discharged on S
1 CONC eptember 12, 1864 (see muster rolls in the New Mexico Archives).  Matias Contreras had been commisioned as a first Lieutenant on November 13, 1861.  Jose Miguel Hermenegildo Salas was dead by 1920.
1 CONT
1 CONT Maria de Agueda de Jesus Contreras was burried in Contreras (Los Ranchos de La Joya located just south of La Joya) on February 6, 1888.
